            "caption": "Psi Irq: Warning Avg10",
            "description": "WARN threshold for the interrupt pressure, in percent of wall clock time, measured over the last ten seconds. Catches a burst that the one minute average smooths away, at the price of alerting on a stall that is over before anybody looks. Supports Nagios ranges. Example: `40` alerts where interrupt handling took four of the last ten seconds. Default: no warning threshold",
            "datatype": "Icinga\\Module\\Director\\DataType\\DataTypeString",
